From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Haiku 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 07:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Lock a package by its install directory

Two instances of one package, such as ld64 and ld64#1, can install into
one install directory, and each held a lock of its own: the lock was
package.lock in the instance's cache folder, and the two folders differ.
Their installs then ran at once into that directory. ld -v reported a
malformed Mach-o file, and another instance's tar extraction and lipo
move failed.

The lock is now a file beside the install directory, <installdir>.lock,
so the instance that comes second waits for the first one. It then reads
the manifest the first one wrote, and does not install again.

Changes-build-output: no

---
 xmake/core/package/package.lua | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xmake/core/package/package.lua b/xmake/core/package/package.lua
index eee2972..19326db 100644
--- a/xmake/core/package/package.lua
+++ b/xmake/core/package/package.lua
@@ -821,11 +821,15 @@ function _instance:use_external_includes()
     return external
 end
 
--- get the filelock of the whole package directory
+-- get the filelock of the install directory: the instances of one package
+-- that install into the same directory share it, so one of them waits for
+-- the other instead of installing into the directory at the same time
 function _instance:filelock()
     local filelock = self._FILELOCK
     if filelock == nil then
-        filelock = io.openlock(path.join(self:cachedir(), "package.lock"))
+        local lockfile = self:installdir() .. ".lock"
+        os.mkdir(path.directory(lockfile))
+        filelock = io.openlock(lockfile)
         if not filelock then
             os.raise("cannot create filelock for package(%s)!", self:name())
         end
